WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.005 --> 00:00:02.529
[MUSIC]

00:00:02.529 --> 00:00:04.220
All strategic leaders face

00:00:04.220 --> 00:00:05.103
complexity in

00:00:05.103 --> 00:00:07.316
their competitive environments.

00:00:07.316 --> 00:00:10.312
What you see is an enormous variety

00:00:10.312 --> 00:00:13.619
of potentially disruptive processes

00:00:13.619 --> 00:00:16.409
going on that really exacerbate

00:00:16.409 --> 00:00:19.521
the challenges that leaders face.

00:00:19.521 --> 00:00:21.058
[MUSIC] What leaders need to do is

00:00:21.058 --> 00:00:22.225
have a set of skills for

00:00:22.225 --> 00:00:23.639
diagnosing the challenges

00:00:23.639 --> 00:00:24.999
that they're tackling.

00:00:24.999 --> 00:00:26.401
And also then being able to

00:00:26.401 --> 00:00:28.388
translate that into an action plan.

00:00:28.388 --> 00:00:29.691
&gt;&gt; What I'd like to do is to

00:00:29.691 --> 00:00:31.384
get out how my business unit can

00:00:31.384 --> 00:00:33.470
contribute to my company's strategy

00:00:33.470 --> 00:00:34.382
and align with my

00:00:34.382 --> 00:00:36.157
company's long-term goals.

00:00:36.157 --> 00:00:37.481
&gt;&gt; The main focus of this

00:00:37.481 --> 00:00:39.026
program is on the issue of

00:00:39.026 --> 00:00:40.577
what we call alignment.

00:00:40.577 --> 00:00:42.708
How do I align my strategy to my

00:00:42.708 --> 00:00:44.762
competitive environment?

00:00:44.762 --> 00:00:45.844
And how do I align my

00:00:45.844 --> 00:00:47.538
organizational design to the

00:00:47.538 --> 00:00:49.714
strategy that I'm trying to pursue?

00:00:49.714 --> 00:00:51.499
&gt;&gt; What is the right leadership?

00:00:51.499 --> 00:00:52.554
And what works and

00:00:52.554 --> 00:00:53.824
what doesn't work?

00:00:53.824 --> 00:00:54.911
&gt;&gt; Great organizations

00:00:54.911 --> 00:00:56.784
are well-aligned organizations.

00:00:56.784 --> 00:00:58.901
We really bring together faculty

00:00:58.901 --> 00:01:01.017
who have devoted their careers to

00:01:01.017 --> 00:01:02.756
understanding the kinds of

00:01:02.756 --> 00:01:04.805
challenges that leaders face.

00:01:04.805 --> 00:01:06.509
&gt;&gt; These are the guys that wrote

00:01:06.509 --> 00:01:08.355
the cases and we're in the room

00:01:08.355 --> 00:01:10.059
with the people who worked in

00:01:10.059 --> 00:01:12.191
the companies so it's fantastic.

00:01:12.191 --> 00:01:13.772
&gt;&gt; Their innovation in the world

00:01:13.772 --> 00:01:14.911
right now is centered

00:01:14.911 --> 00:01:16.240
out of Silicon Valley and

00:01:16.240 --> 00:01:17.959
I see Stanford as a hub for that.

00:01:17.959 --> 00:01:19.503
&gt;&gt; One of the great things about

00:01:19.503 --> 00:01:21.305
EPSO is the incredible diversity

00:01:21.305 --> 00:01:23.107
of participants, participants

00:01:23.107 --> 00:01:24.779
from all over the world from all

00:01:24.779 --> 00:01:26.791
different kinds of organizations.

00:01:26.791 --> 00:01:27.794
So much of the benefit of

00:01:27.794 --> 00:01:29.250
the program comes from the lessons

00:01:29.250 --> 00:01:30.454
that you learn from people in

00:01:30.454 --> 00:01:31.419
different contexts.

00:01:31.419 --> 00:01:32.948
Successful leadership is

00:01:32.948 --> 00:01:35.244
not about cookie-cutter solutions.

00:01:35.244 --> 00:01:37.061
We really want to take you away

00:01:37.061 --> 00:01:39.170
from just feeding your standard,

00:01:39.170 --> 00:01:40.697
here's what all the best

00:01:40.697 --> 00:01:42.223
companies do, to saying

00:01:42.223 --> 00:01:44.040
let's give you the ability to

00:01:44.040 --> 00:01:45.876
build your own solution set.

00:01:45.876 --> 00:01:47.640
&gt;&gt; Each person came with different

00:01:47.640 --> 00:01:48.560
perspectives.

00:01:48.560 --> 00:01:50.964
&gt;&gt; The information on this program

00:01:50.964 --> 00:01:53.011
will help me become a better

00:01:53.011 --> 00:01:53.730
leader.

00:01:53.730 --> 00:01:56.137
&gt;&gt; Was a really well-rounded global

00:01:56.137 --> 00:01:57.382
experience I will

00:01:57.382 --> 00:01:59.626
treasure it the rest of my life.

00:01:59.626 --> 00:02:01.339
[MUSIC]

